      "qty": 34,
      "note": "usually supplied with the SG90; measure your servo's tab hole spacing and drill the bed"
    },
    {
      "item": "M3 screw (stand to bench)",
      "qty": 4
    },
    {
      "item": "Braided line for tendons",
      "qty": 30,
      "note": "flexor and extensor per driven joint; 1.6 mm channels"
    },
    {
      "item": "PTFE tube (tendon sheath)",
      "qty": 1,
      "note": "cut one sheath per tendon run from the bed to the palm"
    },
    {
      "item": "Elastic cord or torsion spring (finger return)",
      "qty": 5
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Kinematics only: tendon stretch, friction and grip force are not simulated; the tip joints follow the middle joints by fixed ratios (0.7 fingers, 0.9 thumb).",
    "17 servos need their own 5 V supply (the template uses a bench supply) with its ground shared by both boards.",
    "The SG90 pockets are the case outline plus 0.2 mm per side; the tab screw holes are not in a drawing we could read — mark them from your servos.",
    "Board U1 drives flexion and the thumb (11 servos), U2 spread and wrist (6): the Arduino Servo library runs at most 12 servos on an Uno."
  ]
